WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.688
Unit 2 is Migrations A and B, by hand.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:09.050
In Migration A, a user account to
a G M S A, watch for the order.

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.113
There's one K D S root key for the
forest, and the domain controllers wait

4
00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:19.175
up to ten hours from its creation before
they allow a G M S A to be created.

5
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:23.975
Then you create the G M S A, install
it and test it on every host.

6
00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:28.500
Then you switch the workload and move
the S P N's in one change window.

7
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.412
After a clean thirty days in parallel,
the old account is disabled and moved.

8
00:00:33.412 --> 00:00:38.433
Migration B, a user account to a D
M S A, starts with Learn's limits:

9
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:42.863
every machine that uses the
account must support D M S A.

10
00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:46.337
Then you create, start, wait and complete.

11
00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:49.499
Learn says to wait at
least two ticket lifetimes;

12
00:00:49.499 --> 00:00:51.949
the program's thirty days covers four.

13
00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:56.413
Learn's D M S A page says never
to delete the original account.

14
00:00:56.413 --> 00:00:58.656
Then skim the guide's special cases,

15
00:00:58.656 --> 00:01:03.050
and stop on failover clusters and
Microsoft Entra Domain Services.
